SUMMARY:Python Toronto September Meetup: September 23 at Fulfil
DESCRIPTION:Python Toronto\nPython Toronto is back! Join us for our Septem
 ber meetup at **Fulfil**\, hosted in the Industrious common area at **30 A
 delaide Street East (near Yonge/Adelaide)** on Wednesday\, September 23\, 
 2026 at 6:00pm!\n\nIf you are interested in giving a talk\, we'd love to h
 ave you! Please fill out this form – [Submit a Python Toronto talk](http
 s://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSfpNKB0Sbs893xp72M4TxmYGrTyLm4Nh1SSXn
 CqChP9mx6_9A/viewform?usp=header)! Talks are typically short\, 5 to 10 min
 utes\, and up to 20 minutes if you've really got something nice to present
 \, and on any topic that would be interesting to a room of Python people. 
 This can be a Python library that has helped you\, a research paper you've
  enjoyed\, or an interesting application of AI.\n\nThe Python meetup is a 
 casual\, community-oriented meetup hosted by companies that use Python in 
 Toronto. Talks are short\, informal\, and sometimes ad-hoc.\nSpace is limi
 ted! Register now to hold your spot.\n\n**When / Where**\n\n* When: Septem
 ber 23\, 2026\, 5:30pm to 8:30pm. Talks will begin around 6:00pm.\n* Where
 : Fulfil - Industrious common area\, 30 Adelaide Street East\, Toronto\, O
 N (near Yonge/Adelaide)\n\nCome early to enjoy snacks and drinks provided.
 \n\n**Code of Conduct**\nPython Toronto is dedicated to providing a welcom
 ing\, harassment-free experience for everyone\, regardless of gender\, gen
 der identity and expression\, age\, sexual orientation\, disability\, phys
 ical appearance\, body size\, race\, ethnicity\, religion (or lack thereof
 )\, or technology choices. We do not tolerate harassment of any form. Sexu
 al language and imagery is not appropriate for this venue\, including talk
 s\, workshops\, parties\, Twitter and other online media. Meetup participa
 nts violating these rules may be sanctioned or expelled from the meetup (w
 ithout a refund where applicable) at the discretion of the meetup organize
 rs. Please email elaine@eswong.ca to report any issues.
